messages.desktop.git.resolve_prompt:
Pulling {upstream} stopped on merge conflicts in:
{files}

Resolve each file: keep what both sides meant to do, remove every conflict marker, and make sure it still builds and its tests pass. Then stage each resolved file with git add. Don't commit or complete the merge: I'll review it and complete it on the Changes page.

messages.desktop.git.resolve_prompt_rebase:
Rebasing onto {upstream} stopped on conflicts in:
{files}

In a rebase, git's "ours" is {upstream} and "theirs" is my commit being replayed. Resolve each file: keep what both sides meant to do, remove every conflict marker, and make sure it still builds. Then stage each resolved file with git add. Don't run git rebase --continue: I'll review it and continue on the Changes page.

messages.desktop.git.resolve_prompt_merge:
Merging {branch} into {current} stopped on merge conflicts in:
{files}

Resolve each file: keep what both sides meant to do, remove every conflict marker, and make sure it still builds and its tests pass. Then stage each resolved file with git add. Don't commit or complete the merge: I'll review it and complete it on the Changes page.
